# Interpreter-throw closure item 6, the callable-merge adapter (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md; Codex, REPLY
# FABLE-STATUS-20261011-08): a held call `(w: 1)` is a call whose callee is dynamic; its model's throw -- here the
# implicit `convert`, the initializer edge refusing -1 -- comes back through the adapter as the model's status and the
# holder's caller, on the status channel by its held call, catches it with its own handler (before: "lmx: invariant:
# a callable merge call failed", abort).  Exit 7; 6 would mean the model completed.
fn: conv (int: y; int: x) int
    int: neg 0 - x
    size_t: s (neg)
    return: y + x

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(y: k; conv)

fn: user () int
    @: w wrap(5)
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: (w: 1)
    ---
    catch: convert ()
        got: 7
return: got

int: r user()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
